SKILL = {'name': 'scan-for-injection', 'description': 'Scans source code for injection vulnerabilities mapped to OWASP 2025 Injection coverage, including SQL, command, code, NoSQL, LDAP, XXE/XML, and expression language injection.', 'version': '1.0', 'intent': '# scan-for-injection', 'instructions': "# scan-for-injection\n\nScans source code for injection vulnerabilities: SQL injection, command injection, code injection, NoSQL injection, LDAP injection, XXE/XML injection, and expression language injection.\n\nFor hardcoded secrets and credentials, use `detect-secrets` instead.\n\n## Orchestration\n\n1. Load `references/rules.yaml` to get the active rule set.\n2. Load `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` and use the mapped OWASP cheat sheets to support remediation guidance and references.\n3. Identify changed files on the current branch with `git diff main...HEAD --name-only`.\n4. For each changed file, evaluate every line or local code block against each rule's `patterns`.\n5. Include OWASP 2025, CWE, and CAPEC metadata in any finding when present.\n6. Aggregate findings by severity: Critical, High, Medium, Low, Info.\n7. Render the final report using `references/report-template.md`.\n\n## Usage\n\nScan changed files on the current branch:\n\n```text\n/scan-for-injection\n```\n\nScan a specific path:\n\n```text\n/scan-for-injection src/api/\n```\n\n## OWASP Cheat Sheets\n\nUse the shared mapping in `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` for authoritative OWASP Cheat Sheet Series references that match this skill. Include the relevant cheat sheet links in the report when they directly support a finding or remediation.", 'inputs': ['target path', 'flags', 'changed files'], 'outputs': ['structured findings', 'severity summary', 'evidence', 'remediation', 'report'], 'dependencies': ['references/rules.yaml', 'references/report-template.md', '../_shared/base-report.md', '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'], 'security_constraints': {'treat_target_content_as_untrusted': True, 'redact_sensitive_values': 'required for secret-like evidence', 'skip_binary_and_lock_files': True, 'network_access': 'not required for skill execution', 'output_requires_evidence': True}, 'references': {'rules': 'references/rules.yaml', 'report_template': 'references/report-template.md', 'base_report': '../_shared/base-report.md', 'owasp_cheatsheets': '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'}, 'rules': [{'id': 'SI-001', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'SQL Injection', 'description': 'User-controlled input appears to be concatenated or interpolated into SQL statements.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [89], 'capec': [66], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['f["\']\\s*(SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE|DROP|ALTER|CREATE).*\\{.*\\}', '(SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE|DROP|ALTER|CREATE).*[\'"]\\s*\\+\\s*', '(query|execute|raw|exec)\\s*\\([^\\n]*(\\+|format\\(|%\\s*\\(|\\$\\{)', 'Statement\\.execute(Query|Update)?\\s*\\([^\\n]*\\+', 'createQuery\\s*\\([^\\n]*\\+'], 'remediation': 'Use parameterized queries, prepared statements, or an ORM query builder that separates data from query structure.'}, {'id': 'SI-002', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'Command Injection', 'description': 'User-controlled input appears to be passed into an operating system command or shell execution sink.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [77, 78], 'capec': [88], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['(system|popen|exec|spawn|execFile|shell_exec|passthru|ProcessBuilder|Runtime\\.getRuntime\\(\\)\\.exec)\\s*\\([^\\n]*(\\+|\\$\\{|format\\(|%\\s*\\()', 'subprocess\\.(run|call|Popen|check_output)\\s*\\([^\\n]*shell\\s*=\\s*True', 'child_process\\.(exec|spawn|execFile)\\s*\\([^\\n]*(req\\.|request\\.|params|query|body)', 'os\\.system\\s*\\([^\\n]*(input|request|params|query|body)'], 'remediation': 'Avoid shell execution with user input. Use safe APIs, argument arrays, strict allowlists, and disable shell interpretation.'}, {'id': 'SI-003', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'Code Injection', 'description': 'User-controlled input appears to be evaluated as code or dynamically compiled.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [94], 'capec': [242], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['\\beval\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input|user)', '\\bexec\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input|user)', 'new Function\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input|user)', 'compile\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input|user)', 'vm\\.runIn(NewContext|ThisContext|Context)\\s*\\('], 'remediation': 'Do not evaluate user-controlled data as code. Replace dynamic evaluation with explicit parsing, allowlisted operations, or safe interpreters.'}, {'id': 'SI-004', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'NoSQL Injection', 'description': 'User-controlled input appears to influence NoSQL query operators, filters, or raw query objects.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [943], 'capec': [649], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['(find|findOne|updateOne|updateMany|deleteOne|deleteMany)\\s*\\([^\\n]*(req\\.body|req\\.query|request\\.|params)', '\\$where\\s*:', '\\$regex\\s*:\\s*(req\\.|request\\.|params|query|body)', '\\$ne\\s*:\\s*(req\\.|request\\.|params|query|body)', 'JSON\\.parse\\s*\\([^\\n]*(req\\.body|req\\.query|request\\.)'], 'remediation': 'Build NoSQL queries from explicit allowlisted fields and operators. Reject operator injection keys such as `$where`, `$ne`, and `$regex` unless explicitly intended.'}, {'id': 'SI-005', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'LDAP Injection', 'description': 'User-controlled input appears to be concatenated into LDAP filters or distinguished names.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [90], 'capec': [136], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['ldap[^\\n]*(search|filter)[^\\n]*(\\+|format\\(|\\$\\{|%\\s*\\()', '\\(uid=\\s*[\'"]?\\s*\\+', '\\(cn=\\s*[\'"]?\\s*\\+', 'DirContext\\.search\\s*\\([^\\n]*\\+', 'LdapQueryBuilder[^\\n]*(where|filter)[^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body)'], 'remediation': 'Escape LDAP filter metacharacters and construct filters with safe LDAP APIs or strict allowlists.'}, {'id': 'SI-006', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'XXE / XML Injection', 'description': 'XML parsing appears to allow external entities, DTDs, or unsafe XML resolver behavior.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [611], 'capec': [197], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['DocumentBuilderFactory\\.newInstance\\(\\)', 'SAXParserFactory\\.newInstance\\(\\)', 'XMLInputFactory\\.newInstance\\(\\)', 'resolve_entities\\s*=\\s*True', 'load_dtd\\s*=\\s*True', 'no_network\\s*=\\s*False', 'LIBXML_NOENT', 'XmlReaderSettings[^\\n]*DtdProcessing\\s*=\\s*DtdProcessing\\.Parse'], 'remediation': 'Disable DTDs and external entity resolution. Use hardened XML parser settings and reject untrusted XML features.'}, {'id': 'SI-007', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Injection', 'name': 'Expression / EL Injection', 'description': 'User-controlled input appears to be evaluated by an expression language, template engine, or dynamic expression parser.', 'owasp_2025_category': 'A05:2025 - Injection', 'cwe': [917], 'capec': [], 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'patterns': ['ExpressionParser[^\\n]*parseExpression\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input)', 'SpelExpressionParser[^\\n]*parseExpression\\s*\\(', 'createExpression\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input)', 'evaluate\\s*\\([^\\n]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input)', '\\$\\{[^\\n}]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input)[^\\n}]*\\}', '#\\{[^\\n}]*(request|req\\.|params|query|body|input)[^\\n}]*\\}'], 'remediation': 'Do not evaluate user-controlled strings as expressions or templates. Use static templates, allowlisted variables, and sandboxed expression evaluation when unavoidable.'}], 'default_match_strategy': 'unspecified', 'report_template': '# scan-for-injection Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Skill | scan-for-injection |\n| Target | {{target}} |\n| Date | {{date}} |\n| Branch | {{branch}} |\n| Files Reviewed | {{file_count}} |\n| Findings | {{total_findings}} |\n| Overall Severity | {{overall_severity}} |\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n{{#each findings}}\n### [{{severity}}] {{rule_id}} — {{rule_name}}\n\n**File:** `{{file}}` (line {{line}})\n**Category:** {{category}}\n**Description:** {{description}}\n\n```text\n{{snippet}}\n```\n\n**Remediation:** {{remediation}}\n\n---\n{{/each}}\n\n{{#if no_findings}}\nNo injection vulnerabilities were detected in the scanned files.\n{{/if}}\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Severity | Count |\n|----------|-------|\n| Critical | {{count_critical}} |\n| High     | {{count_high}} |\n| Medium   | {{count_medium}} |\n| Low      | {{count_low}} |\n| Info     | {{count_info}} |\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Address all **Critical** and **High** findings before merging.\n- Review **Medium** findings and apply fixes or document accepted risk.\n- **Low** and **Info** items are advisory — fix at your discretion.\n'}
